<title>FRANCE: Christian Dior pre-exceptional up 10 pct.</title>
<headline>Christian Dior pre-exceptional up 10 pct.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Christian Dior said its 1996 profit before exceptionals and goodwill amortisation was up 10 percent to 1.183 billion francs due to a rise in results at LVMH and Christian Dior Couture as well as lower financial charges at Christian Dior SA.</p>
<p>However, it took an exceptional charge of 558 million francs reflecting a restructuring of LVMH assets and mainly the sale of Guinness shares.</p>
<p>Sales at fashion house Christian Dior Couture were up 18.8 percent to 1.225 billion fancs and the net income was up 46 percent to 108 million.</p>
</text>
